00:00:02.230 --> 00:00:04.710 align:start position:0%
the breakthrough announced in a tweet  from israeli prime minister yeh lapid a  defining moment for the two states that  used to cooperate in military and other  spheres but who over ten years had  become estranged  and the turkish foreign minister malu  ciao was quick to confirm the  development  among the steps we planned to normalize  relations there was also the  reappointment of respective ambassadors  if you remember we made a statement in  the news conference we held with mr  lapid that we started work on the  appointment of ambassadors  such a positive step came from israel as  a result of these efforts and as turkey  we also decided to appoint an ambassador  to israel to tel aviv  relations between the two countries  soared after israel attacked gaza in  2008 killing more than a thousand  palestinians but it was the gaza  flotilla raid in 2010 that fully severed  ties between the two countries israeli  troops attacked the flotilla which was  carrying humanitarian aid for gaza in  international waters killing nine  turkish citizens  since then diplomatic ties have been  virtually non-existent  in one year there will be a presidential  elections here in turkey but with  inflation at more than 70 percent ankara  wants to attract investments from  regional countries there are security  challenges too in syria and the eastern  mediterranean basin turkey sees israel  as a strong player and for israel turkey  is seen as a balancing power in a region  threatened by iran  the final push to man relations started  last year  in march israeli president isaac herzog  visited turkey and met turkish president  recep tayyip erdogan two months later  turkish foreign minister joshua visited  tel aviv  the final major stepped over  normalization of relations was when  israeli prime minister yeh lapid visited  ankara in june it was during that trip  that the two sides agreed on a road map  to fully restore diplomatic ties  however turkey also made it clear that  it will not compromise when it comes to  supporting the palestinian cows  herzegovina  we have always said we will continue to  defend the rights of palestine jerusalem  and gaza and it's important that our  messages are conveyed directly at the  ambassadorial level in tel aviv  that support for palestinians remains a  sensitive issue and even with the full  restoration of diplomatic ties is likely  to remain a contentious difference  between the two countries  resource al jazeera istanbul
 

